    "Business",
    "What does business travel insurance cover?",
    "Check whether you already have cover",
    "How is business travel insurance different?",
    "Cover for activities on your business trip",
    "Annual versus single-trip insurance",
    "Tegan Oldfield",
    "3 August 2023 | Updated 4 February 2026 | 5 minute read",
    "Travel insurance might not be the first thing that comes to mind when planning a business trip. But having the right policy could be helpful if your journey is delayed, cancelled or if you lose your luggage!",
    "Here’s everything you need to know about choosing the right business travel insurance.",
    "Business travel insurance should cover a range of things.",
    "Gadgets like laptops and phones are often an important part of travelling for business. If you’re taking a few high-value tech items, adding gadget insurance to your policy will cover your gadgets if they’re lost, stolen or damaged on your trip.",
    "Remember to check if your insurer covers items owned by the business, or only items that you own.",
    "Also, you back up any essential data on an external hard drive. Carry it in a separate bag or leave it at home.",
    "Most policies won't cover you for lost data - so if a business contract is riding on a presentation that's on a lost laptop, you could be in trouble! That's why it's important you back everything up.",
    "Cancelled or delayed flights could be an issue if you have important meetings.",
    "A good travel insurance policy includes protection for these types of disruption, paying for additional accommodation and travel if your journey doesn’t go to plan.",
    "In some cases, you can also recover the costs of unused deposits, hotels, excursions, or other pre-booked expenses from your insurer.",
    "If you have to cancel your business trip because you get ill or injured, you should get your money back for your flights and accommodation.",
    "Bear in mind that you might need to get proof from a doctor that you’re unfit to travel.",
    "Also, if you become seriously ill while on your business trip, a travel insurance policy will pay for emergency medical treatment and repatriation (getting you home).",
    "Some companies offer insurance as part of their employment package, so check that you’re not already covered before taking out travel insurance.",
    "If you’re self-employed, then you’ll need to arrange your own travel insurance.",
    "If you’re working with a business who’s paying for your travel and accommodation, they might organise a travel insurance policy for you also.",
    "You can find specific policies tailored to the needs of business travellers. But generally, standard travel insurance policies can be used for both holidays and business trips.",
    "Check the exclusions for business use in your policy. Our policies cover you for both leisure and business trips (excluding any manual work), but other insurers might not.",
    "Your business trip might also involve some networking and socialising activities.",
    "If you’re playing golf with potential clients for example, golf equipment is covered on your standard policy.",
    "We cover you for personal accidents and liability when doing lots of different sports and leisure activities, including:",
    "golf",
    "cycling",
    "fishing",
    "yachting (as long as it’s inside territorial waters)",
    "If you're skiing or snowboarding, you can upgrade your cover to include winter sports insurance.",
    "If you travel abroad for business trips several times a year, an annual travel insurance policy might be more cost-effective.",
    "As well as working out cheaper than multiple single-trip policies, an annual policy means you can arrange business trips without worrying about sorting insurance each time.",
    "Our annual multi-trip insurance covers you for unlimited trips lasting up to 31 days at a time as standard.",
